The SVG files in this directory are icons from the vscode-icons project.

    Source:  https://github.com/vscode-icons/vscode-icons
    Tag:     v12.19.0
    Icons:   Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International
             (CC BY-SA 4.0) — https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
    Credit:  © vscode-icons contributors
             https://github.com/vscode-icons/vscode-icons/graphs/contributors

NO CHANGES WERE MADE. Every file here is byte-identical to the file of the same
name at that tag; `SOURCE.md` records a sha256 for each one so that claim can be
checked rather than believed. This matters legally, not only tidily: an edited
icon would be Adapted Material under CC BY-SA and its ShareAlike term would
reach whatever it is combined with. The rest of pdmux is Apache-2.0, so nothing
in this directory may be recoloured, re-pathed, minified or merged into a sprite
— see the note beside `.pdmux-files-icon` in `../../styles.css`.

Upstream describes its licensing in three parts, and the third one applies to
most of the files here: "The source code is licensed under the MIT license. The
icons are licensed under the Creative Commons - ShareAlike (CC BY-SA) license.
Branded icons are licensed under their copyright license."

BRANDED ICONS. Several of these are the trademarks of the projects and companies
whose file types they mark (for example Python, Rust, Docker, npm). They are
used here for the one purpose a file manager's icon serves — identifying which
kind of file a row is — and no endorsement or affiliation is claimed or implied.
Each remains the property of its owner under its owner's terms.
